WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:03.500
(Episode 1)

3
00:20.660 --> 00:21.660
Mango shaved ice!

4
00:21.820 --> 00:22.820
Thanks for waiting.

5
00:25.080 --> 00:26.680
- Enjoy. - Thank you!

6
00:36.920 --> 00:38.140
Business is pretty slow.

7
00:38.240 --> 00:39.240
Odajima.

8
00:40.040 --> 00:41.440
Where are all the girls in bikinis?

9
00:42.330 --> 00:43.000
How is it?

10
00:43.290 --> 00:44.260
Yeah, it's delicious.

11
00:44.261 --> 00:46.280
- Not a single one. - Why is that?

12
00:46.480 --> 00:47.660
This is Okinawa.

13
00:47.720 --> 00:48.720
It's a resort island.

14
00:49.080 --> 00:51.000
It's nothing like the mainland. Nothing like it.

15
00:55.580 --> 00:57.020
Did I just say "the mainland"?

16
00:58.480 --> 00:59.480
You did.

17
01:01.520 --> 01:03.980
Guess that makes me a real islander, sa~.

18
01:04.660 --> 01:05.880
Did I use "sa" right?

19
01:07.340 --> 01:08.340
Who knows.

20
01:08.860 --> 01:09.960
Pun on "sa", huh?

21
01:13.140 --> 01:14.340
You're getting better at this.

22
01:14.560 --> 01:16.040
Don't go getting funnier than me!

23
01:16.240 --> 01:17.480
It was an accident.

24
01:19.160 --> 01:20.400
My stomach hurts from laughing.

25
01:32.960 --> 01:34.400
All right, all right, don't cry.

26
01:35.260 --> 01:37.400
Just dust off the dirty part, and it's still good.

27
01:38.220 --> 01:39.220
Watch this.

28
01:43.400 --> 01:44.400
Whoa...

29
01:44.420 --> 01:45.520
It's full of sand!

30
01:45.580 --> 01:46.580
You can't eat this!

31
01:46.840 --> 01:47.840
Gross!

32
01:50.540 --> 01:52.400
- Ugly! - Huh?

33
01:52.480 --> 01:54.600
- Ugly! Ugly! - Handsome! Handsome!

34
01:54.800 --> 01:55.919
Ugly! Ugly!

35
01:55.920 --> 01:57.160
Handsome! Handsome! Handsome!

36
01:58.180 --> 02:00.036
Handsome! Handsome! Handsome! Handsome! Handsome!

37
02:00.060 --> 02:02.200
Say it again! Say handsome!

38
02:04.740 --> 02:05.840
I still think back to it.

39
02:09.520 --> 02:10.520
Odajima.

40
02:11.380 --> 02:12.990
Go kill Kataoka.

41
02:21.560 --> 02:23.100
Killing this man

42
02:24.300 --> 02:25.700
was once my sole reason for living.

43
02:36.960 --> 02:37.960
Kataoka-san!

44
02:53.160 --> 02:54.560
- Here. - Thanks.

45
02:55.780 --> 02:56.780
Take it.

46
02:56.900 --> 02:59.060
- On the house. - Thank you!

47
03:03.720 --> 03:04.460
Yummy!

48
03:04.461 --> 03:05.819
Good, huh?

49
03:05.820 --> 03:06.820
Yeah!

50
03:07.560 --> 03:08.560
Look, an airplane!

51
03:11.620 --> 03:12.799
You like planes?

52
03:12.800 --> 03:13.800
Uh-huh!

53
03:14.920 --> 03:15.920
Yet here we are.

54
03:16.940 --> 03:18.040
Side by side,

55
03:18.640 --> 03:19.800
looking up at the same sky.

56
03:39.340 --> 03:40.920
Thank you so much!

57
03:42.220 --> 03:43.940
Island men drink after they dance!

58
03:44.390 --> 03:45.680
I hear ya!

59
03:46.120 --> 03:47.120
Everyone,

60
03:47.620 --> 03:48.620
cheers!

61
03:53.060 --> 03:55.870
Yeah! Let's drink up tonight!

62
03:56.940 --> 03:57.940
Cheers!

63
04:08.240 --> 04:09.240
Odajima.

64
04:09.720 --> 04:11.040
Have a drink, too.

65
04:12.410 --> 04:13.410
Sure.

66
04:20.700 --> 04:21.700
Excuse me.

67
04:22.300 --> 04:23.080
I'll have an ice cream soda, please.

68
04:23.130 --> 04:24.299
An ice cream soda? Seriously?!

69
04:24.300 --> 04:25.740
Coming right up! One ice cream soda!

70
04:25.840 --> 04:27.180
You told me to get a drink.

71
04:28.180 --> 04:29.780
You're such a buzzkill.

72
04:31.440 --> 04:35.870
A stiff bastard like you needs a drink to loosen up.

73
04:36.940 --> 04:39.520
Listen. The only things that should be hard in this world

74
04:40.280 --> 04:41.280
are rice crackers

75
04:42.060 --> 04:43.260
and "that thing."

76
04:44.400 --> 04:45.400
That thing?

77
04:45.540 --> 04:46.540
Really?

78
04:46.580 --> 04:47.580
Damn straight.

79
04:47.800 --> 04:48.800
You know, "that thing."

80
04:49.760 --> 04:50.760
Hey.

81
04:50.800 --> 04:52.000
Sorry to keep you waiting.

82
04:57.280 --> 04:58.280
Odajima.

83
04:59.100 --> 05:00.100
Yes?

84
05:01.500 --> 05:02.700
Let me have a sip later.

85
05:04.800 --> 05:05.800
Sure.

86
05:06.510 --> 05:09.320
Boss, thanks for always taking care of us.

87
05:09.360 --> 05:11.860
- Thank you, Boss! - I told you, I'm not your boss anymore.

88
05:12.440 --> 05:13.819
How's work at the restaurant?

89
05:13.820 --> 05:18.060
We're just part-timers, but we basically run the place.

90
05:18.400 --> 05:20.219
I've gotten real good at making mozuku tempura!

91
05:20.220 --> 05:21.560
Oh, not bad at all.

92
05:22.100 --> 05:24.680
- Keep it up. - Yes, sir! Back to work!

93
05:26.500 --> 05:28.039
Handsome! One more order of sea grapes!

94
05:28.040 --> 05:29.480
Right away! One order of sea grapes!

95
05:32.860 --> 05:34.480
Look at those two.

96
05:35.340 --> 05:37.160
They were just petty punks when we first met.

97
05:38.160 --> 05:39.380
Take us with you!

98
05:39.480 --> 05:40.760
- Exactly! - Boss!

99
05:40.860 --> 05:42.460
- Pull over! - Don't leave us behind!

100
05:42.500 --> 05:43.500
Boss!

101
05:44.800 --> 05:46.040
To think we retired,

102
05:46.580 --> 05:48.960
and they still chased us all the way to Okinawa.

103
05:55.420 --> 05:56.420
It's getting late.

104
05:56.980 --> 05:58.680
- Time to head back. - Understood.

105
05:59.560 --> 06:00.900
We're taking off.

106
06:01.320 --> 06:02.660
Kataoka, see you next time.

107
06:03.280 --> 06:04.720
Aya-chan, that was a wonderful song.

108
06:04.900 --> 06:05.540
Thank you.

109
06:05.580 --> 06:07.119
- Come back soon! - Sure, see you later.

110
06:07.120 --> 06:08.120
See you.

111
06:08.960 --> 06:09.960
Thanks for having us.

112
06:16.960 --> 06:18.580
The night breeze feels nice.

113
06:20.500 --> 06:23.060
It's been three years since the boss took us in here in Okinawa.

114
06:25.140 --> 06:27.400
Twenty years in the yakuza, and I never knew.

115
06:28.180 --> 06:29.520
An honest day's work,

116
06:30.040 --> 06:31.460
dinner after sundown,

117
06:32.180 --> 06:33.380
and a good drink.

118
06:37.080 --> 06:38.280
A life like this...

119
06:41.700 --> 06:43.380
I guess this is what happiness feels like.

120
06:47.660 --> 06:49.500
You don't need to stand guard over me anymore.

121
06:50.080 --> 06:51.340
You can have a drink, too.

122
06:53.020 --> 06:54.020
You noticed?

123
06:56.700 --> 06:58.540
It's a curse, being in the yakuza for so long.

124
06:59.226 --> 07:00.946
Can't shake years of conditioning.

125
07:02.440 --> 07:04.520
No matter how much I drink, I can't even get buzzed.

126
07:07.540 --> 07:08.540
Still...

127
07:08.900 --> 07:10.860
I'd kind of like to see you drunk.

128
07:12.820 --> 07:13.820
Right.

129
07:14.040 --> 07:16.630
How about downing a bottle of Awamori next time?

130
07:16.970 --> 07:18.020
No thanks.

131
07:18.180 --> 07:20.820
Come on, such a party pooper.

132
07:21.560 --> 07:22.660
Then Habushu it is.

133
07:23.140 --> 07:25.180
I hear it gets you rock hard.

134
07:26.280 --> 07:27.280
Where?

135
07:28.110 --> 07:29.380
Where?

136
07:30.886 --> 07:31.886
Down "there."

137
08:14.080 --> 08:15.080
A life like this...

138
08:16.740 --> 08:18.160
is what happiness feels like.

139
08:28.090 --> 08:29.270
Kill me.

140
08:40.930 --> 08:42.390
Kill me.

141
08:42.680 --> 08:44.840
- Kill me! - You think you can escape?

142
08:45.220 --> 08:46.299
You're just like me.

143
08:46.300 --> 08:47.680
You will never...

144
08:47.730 --> 08:51.150
never find happiness.

145
09:16.470 --> 09:19.740
I can never be happy.

146
09:21.320 --> 09:22.520
I don't deserve happiness.

147
09:25.440 --> 09:30.240
(Kumakura: Kataoka-san, please contact me as soon as possible.)

148
09:44.920 --> 09:47.420
- Hey, get up! - Please!

149
09:47.740 --> 09:49.170
Don't kill me!

150
09:50.920 --> 09:52.300
Spare my life!

151
09:53.800 --> 09:54.800
Shut up!

152
09:56.740 --> 09:57.840
I'm telling the truth!

153
09:58.180 --> 09:59.540
Please, believe me!

154
10:04.760 --> 10:07.000
All your screaming made me die in the game.

155
10:09.000 --> 10:10.000
I'm begging you!

156
10:10.740 --> 10:11.740
Have mercy!

157
10:23.260 --> 10:24.260
Chairman.

158
10:25.200 --> 10:26.200
Tell me.

159
10:26.960 --> 10:29.360
Do you know the difference between "shameless" and "brazen"?

160
10:30.760 --> 10:31.760
No...

161
10:32.020 --> 10:33.500
I'm not an educated man,

162
10:34.100 --> 10:35.100
so I wouldn't know.

163
10:36.740 --> 10:37.840
Being "brazen"...

164
10:38.920 --> 10:39.960
Even if someone oversteps,

165
10:40.400 --> 10:41.960
somehow you can't completely hate them.

166
10:43.280 --> 10:44.280
However,

167
10:44.810 --> 10:47.390
being "shameless" is just pure greed,

168
10:48.400 --> 10:49.500
or downright deceitful.

169
10:50.340 --> 10:51.340
Ah.

170
10:51.520 --> 10:53.360
Is it because "shameless" means without shame?

171
11:01.480 --> 11:02.480
So you see,

172
11:02.660 --> 11:05.260
cooking the books and then begging for your life...

173
11:07.840 --> 11:09.560
Isn't that utterly shameless?

174
12:15.600 --> 12:17.600
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

175
12:19.490 --> 12:20.730
Morning, Kataoka.

176
12:21.250 --> 12:22.490
We're back again today!

177
12:23.730 --> 12:25.850
I bet you're not getting any shaved ice today either.

178
12:31.730 --> 12:33.949
- Excuse me. - Welcome!

179
12:33.950 --> 12:34.950
Welcome!

180
12:37.970 --> 12:39.370
- Here. - Oh, no...

181
12:40.230 --> 12:41.230
Um...

182
12:41.430 --> 12:44.050
Can I buy a phone charger around here?

183
12:44.760 --> 12:46.000
- A charger? - Yes.

184
12:55.610 --> 12:56.610
You can borrow mine.

185
12:56.860 --> 12:58.020
Really? Are you sure?

186
12:59.190 --> 13:00.370
Thank you so much!

187
13:01.710 --> 13:02.710
Are you here alone?

188
13:05.390 --> 13:07.310
Shin-chan, he's letting us borrow his!

189
13:10.490 --> 13:11.680
Thank you.

190
13:14.210 --> 13:15.930
- Is that your girl, kid? - Yes.

191
13:16.930 --> 13:17.930
And actually,

192
13:18.690 --> 13:19.890
we're getting married soon.

193
13:23.170 --> 13:24.870
- That's on the house. - Huh?

194
13:25.530 --> 13:26.530
Really...?

195
13:26.750 --> 13:28.070
Take good care of her, all right?

196
13:29.990 --> 13:31.060
Thank you, sir!

197
13:32.950 --> 13:34.229
He's so nice.

198
13:34.230 --> 13:35.230
Yeah.

199
13:36.390 --> 13:37.490
He told you to cherish me.

200
13:38.630 --> 13:39.710
I will. I promise.

201
13:41.430 --> 13:42.430
Odajima.

202
13:47.110 --> 13:48.230
Where are all the customers?

203
13:50.910 --> 13:51.910
Not a single one.

204
13:53.190 --> 13:54.390
Boring.

205
13:59.450 --> 14:00.450
Strange.

206
14:00.770 --> 14:01.770
Where did my phone go?

207
14:15.730 --> 14:19.200
(Kumakura: Kataoka-san, please contact me as soon as possible.)

208
14:31.620 --> 14:32.620
Here.

209
14:32.650 --> 14:33.650
Say ahh.

210
14:37.000 --> 14:38.920
We're so slow today.

211
14:45.630 --> 14:46.630
Right this way.

212
14:58.450 --> 14:59.450
Pardon the intrusion.

213
15:00.370 --> 15:01.370
My apologies.

214
15:01.590 --> 15:04.510
The Chairman is out, so I'll be meeting with you instead.

215
15:05.400 --> 15:06.400
I appreciate it.

216
15:07.130 --> 15:08.130
What brings you here?

217
15:10.010 --> 15:11.010
Ihashi-san.

218
15:12.570 --> 15:14.590
Regarding this month's tribute payment...

219
15:19.070 --> 15:20.270
Is there a problem with it?

220
15:21.150 --> 15:22.150
Well...

221
15:23.730 --> 15:24.930
Would it be possible

222
15:25.690 --> 15:27.110
to give us a few extra days?

223
15:29.430 --> 15:31.330
Is this what the Fourth Leader wants?

224
15:31.790 --> 15:32.890
No.

225
15:36.270 --> 15:37.490
This is on my own accord.

226
15:39.250 --> 15:40.450
That's problematic.

227
15:40.630 --> 15:43.390
Matters like this must be discussed with the Fourth Leader in person.

228
15:45.130 --> 15:46.490
So, Kumakura-san,

229
15:48.110 --> 15:50.530
make sure the payment is made on time.

230
15:56.730 --> 15:57.830
If, by chance,

231
15:58.750 --> 15:59.950
it happens to be late...

232
16:08.970 --> 16:09.970
Understood.

233
16:14.680 --> 16:15.840
Oh, and another thing.

234
16:19.236 --> 16:22.994
The Chairman asked me to convey that the Fourth Leader

235
16:23.018 --> 16:26.426
should attend executive meetings once in a while.

236
16:36.610 --> 16:37.610
It's me.

237
16:38.270 --> 16:40.710
What's the status on the revenues from our Awakuma territory?

238
16:43.270 --> 16:44.870
Cut the crap and scrape up the cash now!

239
16:50.920 --> 16:51.920
Boss...

240
16:54.190 --> 16:57.050
Our profits are falling short of expectations.

241
16:59.710 --> 17:02.340
We're running out of working capital.

242
17:02.370 --> 17:03.790
(Two Major Bottlenecks in Awakuma)

243
17:05.130 --> 17:06.430
We're short on cash...

244
17:08.970 --> 17:11.510
"Evaluation pending due to public safety risks."

245
17:13.290 --> 17:15.090
"Investment decisions suspended."

246
17:23.960 --> 17:25.850
Kataoka, we're taking off.

247
17:26.030 --> 17:26.670
Thanks again.

248
17:26.750 --> 17:29.809
- Get home safe. - Kataoka, we'll be back tomorrow!

249
17:29.810 --> 17:31.930
All right. Make sure to buy some shaved ice tomorrow!

250
17:32.770 --> 17:33.970
Look at you grinning.

251
17:37.470 --> 17:38.810
About time to close up.

252
17:41.350 --> 17:42.350
Hm?

253
17:42.890 --> 17:45.450
Odajima?

254
17:47.250 --> 17:48.250
Yes.

255
18:11.970 --> 18:14.010
You've been acting weird all day.

256
18:17.090 --> 18:18.090
Hey.

257
18:34.410 --> 18:37.410
Come to think of it, we got married, but we never had a ceremony.

258
18:38.590 --> 18:39.590
Huh?

259
18:41.430 --> 18:43.270
What kind of wedding would you want?

260
19:30.710 --> 19:34.390
(Kumakura: Apologies for reaching out repeatedly. Please get back to me as soon as possible.)

261
19:38.130 --> 19:39.530
Is that my phone?

262
19:44.010 --> 19:45.010
Huh?

263
19:51.930 --> 19:52.930
This is Kumakura.

264
19:54.150 --> 19:55.570
If things continue like this,

265
19:57.650 --> 19:59.690
the Kirii-gumi will be wiped out by the Koutokukai.

266
20:01.690 --> 20:02.890
I know you've retired,

267
20:03.010 --> 20:06.010
and I have no right to beg you.

268
20:07.530 --> 20:08.730
But Kataoka-san,

269
20:08.810 --> 20:10.070
to save the Kirii-gumi,

270
20:11.250 --> 20:12.350
I beg of you,

271
20:12.930 --> 20:14.030
please come back.

272
20:40.830 --> 20:42.030
Why did you hide this from me?

273
20:45.790 --> 20:46.890
I'm deeply sorry.

274
21:00.590 --> 21:01.590
I'm truly

275
21:02.530 --> 21:03.530
sorry.

276
21:18.410 --> 21:19.410
I keep having

277
21:22.770 --> 21:23.970
the exact same dream.

278
21:29.570 --> 21:31.070
I see the man I killed.

279
21:35.380 --> 21:37.060
He tells me, "Don't think you can escape."

280
21:39.690 --> 21:41.590
"You will never find happiness."

281
21:47.190 --> 21:48.190
Waking up.

282
21:50.180 --> 21:51.180
Working.

283
21:53.230 --> 21:54.230
Eating.

284
21:56.510 --> 21:57.510
Sleeping in the same bed.

285
21:59.790 --> 22:01.250
Living like normal people,

286
22:02.630 --> 22:03.830
spending each day with you.

287
22:07.570 --> 22:08.890
Even after paying a massive price

288
22:11.810 --> 22:13.610
to break ties and buy my freedom,

289
22:16.410 --> 22:17.410
I still feel like

290
22:18.370 --> 22:19.450
I can't go anywhere at all!

291
22:23.610 --> 22:24.610
So, Kataoka-san,

292
22:27.810 --> 22:28.810
at least for you...

293
22:32.570 --> 22:34.250
I wanted at least for you to live freely.

294
23:17.810 --> 23:18.910
You idiot.

295
23:31.320 --> 23:33.550
You're far too stiff.

296
23:35.570 --> 23:37.110
Not that I dislike that about you.

297
23:41.630 --> 23:42.630
Listen, Odajima.

298
23:46.690 --> 23:47.690
We

299
23:50.430 --> 23:51.430
are free.

300
23:54.150 --> 23:56.270
It's because we're free that we can choose not to be.

301
23:57.190 --> 23:59.470
Isn't clinging to freedom just another form of restraint?

302
24:01.270 --> 24:02.350
Odajima.

303
24:04.230 --> 24:05.430
We are free.

304
24:09.030 --> 24:10.590
We can do anything,

305
24:13.230 --> 24:14.630
and go anywhere.

306
24:18.510 --> 24:19.510
Odajima.

307
24:25.070 --> 24:26.070
What is it

308
24:28.840 --> 24:30.090
that you truly desire?

309
24:34.600 --> 24:35.600
Freedom...

310
25:16.750 --> 25:17.750
All right.

311
25:18.560 --> 25:19.560
Let's go.

312
25:26.190 --> 25:27.290
What's wrong, Odajima?

313
25:29.210 --> 25:30.210
Nothing.

314
25:30.750 --> 25:31.750
It's fine.

315
25:35.150 --> 25:37.190
You didn't forget the phone, did you?

316
25:41.190 --> 25:42.190
Kataoka-san.

317
25:42.850 --> 25:44.030
Yeah? What is it?

318
25:45.130 --> 25:46.130
That's not just a phone.

319
25:46.310 --> 25:47.310
It's a smartphone.

320
25:58.030 --> 25:59.030
Hey.

321
25:59.590 --> 26:01.116
How long are we supposed to watch the shop?

322
26:01.140 --> 26:02.610
How should I know, idiot?

323
26:04.190 --> 26:07.620
Probably until the Boss gets back.

324
26:09.290 --> 26:11.570
Not like there are any customers anyway.

325
26:13.550 --> 26:14.550
Tell me about it.

326
26:22.130 --> 26:23.130
Chairman.

327
26:23.650 --> 26:24.970
The Kirii-gumi's payment...

328
26:26.090 --> 26:27.290
I'm afraid it will be delayed.

329
26:33.190 --> 26:34.490
Pulling a stunt like this...

330
26:35.670 --> 26:37.630
How do they plan to settle it?

331
26:46.390 --> 26:47.390
How

332
26:47.450 --> 26:48.450
